course: dictionary
lesson: 13332
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it. «Mia counted the gumdrops in the bag.» Gumdrops can be counted, so here they are sweets.
explain: «Night night, my gumdrop, sleep tight!» Nobody is counting or eating anything. A gumdrop here is a sweet person, used as a loving pet name. This is the informal meaning.
explain: Gumdrops appear in maths too. «Sam sorted the gumdrops by colour, then shared them equally.» Sorting and sharing tell you that gumdrops are things to count in a maths problem.
explain: Ask yourself: does the sweet meaning fit this sentence? If it does not, try the pet name meaning. Swapping in your own meaning is a quick way to check.
fact: A gumdrop is a small, soft, chewy sweet shaped like a little dome.
fact: Gumdrops are usually coated in sugar and are brightly coloured.
fact: «Gumdrop» can also be an informal pet name for a sweet person.
fact: In the US and Canada, gumdrops are often used at parties and for decorating gingerbread houses.
fact: «Gumdrops» is the plural: it means more than one gumdrop.
exercise: «Mia counted the gumdrops in the bag.» What are the gumdrops? | Painted pebbles | A type of bird | *Small, soft, chewy sweets | A kind of cloud
exercise: Grandma says, «Good night, gumdrop!» What does gumdrop mean here? | A rainy day | A small dome-shaped hat | *A sweet person, used as a pet name | A kind of bird
exercise: «Sam sorted the gumdrops by colour.» What is Sam doing? | *Putting them into groups by colour | Hiding them in a box | Painting the bag | Eating all of them quickly
test: Which is the best meaning of gumdrop in «Ana is my little gumdrop, my favourite person»? | *A sweet person, used as a pet name | A party | A paper bag | A sweet food
test: In «The gumdrops were coated in sugar and bright colours», which clue shows they are sweets? | Bright | The | Coated | *Sugar
exam: What clue shows that the gumdrops are countable things in «Lily shared the gumdrops equally between four friends»? | *Shared out equally | Friends | Four | Lily
